# Coding Standards

_Generated by arbiter. Update to match your team's conventions._

## General

- Prefer immutable variables (const/val/final)
- Functions should have a single responsibility
- No magic numbers — use named constants
- Maximum cyclomatic complexity: 15

<% if (language === 'typescript') { %>
## TypeScript

- `strict: true` in tsconfig — mandatory
- No `any` type — use `unknown` and narrow, or create proper types
- Named exports preferred over default exports
- File naming: kebab-case.ts
- Linting: ESLint with `@typescript-eslint` ruleset
- Dead code: Knip (zero unused exports)
- Coverage threshold: 80% lines

<% } %>
<% if (language === 'java' || language === 'kotlin') { %>
## JVM

- Static analysis: SpotBugs — zero HIGH/CRITICAL findings
- Coverage: JaCoCo — 80% line coverage minimum
- Style: Checkstyle — Google Java Style Guide
- No raw types — use generics
- Checked exceptions only when caller must handle them

<% } %>
<% if (language === 'python') { %>
## Python

- Type hints mandatory on all public functions (PEP 484)
- Black + isort for formatting (no manual exceptions)
- pylint/flake8 zero warnings
- Coverage threshold: 80% (pytest-cov)
- Docstrings for all public modules, classes, and functions (Google style)

<% } %>
<% if (language === 'go') { %>
## Go

- `go vet` and `staticcheck` — zero warnings
- `gofmt` applied before every commit
- Error wrapping: `fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)` — no bare `errors.New`
- Coverage threshold: 80% (go test -cover)
- No global mutable state

<% } %>
<% if (language === 'rust') { %>
## Rust

- `clippy` at deny level — zero warnings
- No `unwrap()` in production code — use `?` or handle explicitly
- `rustfmt` applied before every commit
- Coverage threshold: 80% (cargo-tarpaulin or similar)
- Prefer `thiserror` for error types

<% } %>
<% if (governanceLevel === 'L3') { %>
## L3 Governance

- All public APIs must have OpenAPI/Swagger documentation
- Breaking changes require an ADR
- Architectural decision records: `docs/adr/`
- Security review required for any auth, crypto, or external boundary changes

